<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ===========================================================================
  THE INSTAPAY ROW SHIPS WITH ITS BRAND MARK
  ===========================================================================
  Model\PresentationCatalog reads checkout/spartrak_payment/rows and returns []
  when it is unset. Until now nothing set it, so a freshly installed store
  rendered every payment row as a bare Magento title with no artwork — which is
  what Figma 554:10500 draws a mark on, and what a shopper uses to recognise
  the method at a glance.

  A DEFAULT, NOT A HARDCODED VALUE. It seeds core_config_data on install and is
  editable at Stores > Configuration > Sales > Checkout > Payment row
  presentation, per store view. The same reasoning as
  Spartrak_CustomerAddress's optional_zip_countries default.

  `spartrak_instapay` is the method code declared in Spartrak_InstaPay's own
  etc/payment.xml — not a guess. `instapay` is the key of the mark in
  Model\BrandMarks, which resolves it to
  view/frontend/web/images/payment/instapay.png, the asset exported from Figma
  at its original colours.

  ===========================================================================
  WHY ONLY THIS ONE ROW
  ===========================================================================
  Figma's payment step (551:11313) draws four rows: bank card, e-wallets,
  InstaPay and instalments. Only two payment methods actually exist in this
  codebase to attach them to — `spartrak_instapay` and `paymob_payment` — and
  which of Figma's rows the Paymob method represents depends on how that
  gateway is configured for the merchant, so guessing it here would put card
  marks on a wallet row. The wallet and instalment rows have no method at all
  yet. Those get added as rows when their methods are enabled; seeding a row
  for a code that does not exist would be dead configuration.

  ===========================================================================
  NO `description` HERE, DELIBERATELY
  ===========================================================================
  Figma gives each row a line of copy ("إدفع بسهولة ولحظيا" for this one). A
  config.xml default is a single global string that is NOT run through __(),
  so seeding it would print Arabic copy on the English store view too. Copy is
  store-view content and belongs in the admin field, per store view — the same
  content/presentation split as CLAUDE.md section 7. The brand mark is an
  asset, not copy, so it is safe to default.
-->
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Store:etc/config.xsd">
    <default>
        <checkout>
            <spartrak_payment>
                <rows><![CDATA[{"spartrak_instapay":{"method":"spartrak_instapay","brands":["instapay"],"description":""}}]]></rows>
            </spartrak_payment>
        </checkout>
    </default>
</config>
